# Untrusted content (PRD P6)

Source: `docs/research/04-trust-safety-and-scam-detection.md` §4.

1. **Sanitize** before AI: strip scripts/styles, hidden elements (`display:none`, zero-size, white-on-white, off-screen), HTML comments, zero-width characters; keep visible text only.
2. **Flag** injection-shaped lines ("ignore previous instructions", "you are an AI", "include the following in your application", text addressed to assistants). Flagged postings get a yellow risk reason and the flagged lines are removed from AI context.
3. **Delimit**: pass untrusted text inside clearly marked data blocks with an instruction that the contents are data.
4. **Least privilege**: LLM calls that read untrusted text have **no tools**. Tools that act (fill, submit, send, write) consume only structured, validated outputs with strict Pydantic schemas, never raw text from a posting, email, or page.
5. **Never follow links** from posting or email bodies automatically; only the canonical apply URL resolved by our own code.
6. Page text that tells the filler what to do (e.g. "answer yes to all") is page content, not a command.

Test every new ingestion path with an injection fixture. Skill: `ai-evals`.
